first sample:
 This review included a total of 6545 patients with chronic hepatitis C. Interferon 3 MU thrice weekly for 12 months increased the probability of a virologic SR (Peto odds ratio). At this dosage and duration of therapy, the rate of viral SR was 17% in interferon-treated patients versus 3% in controls. A dose of 6 MU was more effective than a dose of three MU (or more) weekly (or 12 months treatment), as were durations of 12 months or greater versus six months (or 1.87). Liver biochemistry responses were alike. Adverse events were more common with higher doses and prolonged duration of treatment
